/*
 * Purchase Management System - Local Storage Mode
 * All application data is stored in the browser's localStorage.
 * No Flask/API/PostgreSQL connection is required for the frontend.
 */
const STORAGE_KEY = 'purchase_management_state_v1';
const AUTH_KEY = 'purchase_management_current_user_v1';
const PURCHASER_TRN = '104508434800';
const DEFAULT_TAX_RATE = 5;
const DEFAULT_PO_TERMS = `Terms & Conditions\n\nLocal Purchase Order — Terms & Conditions\n1. Acceptance of Order\nThis LPO constitutes an offer to purchase the goods/services listed herein, subject to these terms. Acceptance of this order (by delivery, invoice, or written confirmation) constitutes agreement to all terms stated. Any variation to price, quantity, or specification requires prior written approval from the Purchaser.\n2. Pricing\nPrices stated are fixed and firm for the duration of the order unless otherwise agreed in writing. Prices are exclusive of UAE VAT unless stated otherwise, and VAT must be shown separately on the invoice as per FTA requirements. No price escalation is permitted without prior written consent.\n3. Delivery\nGoods/services must be delivered to the specified location, date, and time as stated on the LPO.\nThe Supplier must notify the Purchaser immediately of any anticipated delay.\nDelivery must be accompanied by a delivery note referencing the LPO number.\nPartial deliveries are not accepted unless explicitly authorized.\n4. Late Delivery / Penalty\nIn case of delay not attributable to Force Majeure, the Purchaser reserves the right to charge a penalty (commonly 0.5%–1% of order value per day of delay, capped at 10%), cancel the order, and/or source alternatively at the Supplier's cost.\n5. Inspection & Quality\nAll goods are subject to inspection and testing upon receipt. The Purchaser reserves the right to reject non-conforming goods/services, which must be replaced or corrected by the Supplier at no additional cost within an agreed timeframe.\n6. Invoicing & Payment\nInvoices must reference the LPO number, be TRN-compliant (Tax Registration Number shown), and itemize VAT separately. Payment terms: as specified on the LPO (e.g., 30/60/90 days from invoice date or delivery acceptance). Payments are made via bank transfer to the account specified in the Supplier's registration/invoice. No payment shall be made against an invoice without a valid matching LPO.\n7. Warranty\nThe Supplier warrants that all goods/services are new (unless specified as refurbished), free from defects in material and workmanship, and fit for the intended purpose for a minimum period of [12 months] from delivery/acceptance, or per manufacturer warranty if longer.\n8. Compliance with UAE Law\nThe Supplier shall comply with all applicable UAE federal laws, Dubai Municipality/DED regulations, and relevant free zone authority rules, including labour law, health & safety, customs, and environmental regulations.\n9. Confidentiality\nThe Supplier shall treat all information relating to this order, pricing, and the Purchaser's business as confidential and shall not disclose it to third parties without prior written consent.\n10. Insurance & Liability\nThe Supplier shall maintain adequate insurance (e.g., third-party liability, goods-in-transit) as applicable, and shall indemnify the Purchaser against any loss, damage, or injury arising from defective goods or negligent performance.\n11. Force Majeure\nNeither party shall be liable for delay or failure to perform due to circumstances beyond reasonable control (natural disasters, government action, strikes, etc.), provided the affected party notifies the other promptly and mitigates the impact.\n12. Termination / Cancellation\nThe Purchaser may cancel this LPO, in whole or part, by written notice if the Supplier fails to meet delivery, quality, or compliance requirements, without liability beyond payment for goods/services already accepted.\n13. Ownership & Risk\nTitle and risk in the goods pass to the Purchaser only upon delivery and formal acceptance, unless otherwise agreed.\n14. Assignment\nThe Supplier may not assign or subcontract this order, in whole or part, without the Purchaser's prior written consent.\n15. Dispute Resolution & Governing Law\nThis LPO shall be governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates. Any dispute shall first be resolved amicably; failing that, it shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Dubai Courts (or, if agreed, DIFC-LCIA/DIAC arbitration seated in Dubai).\n16. Anti-Bribery & Ethics\nThe Supplier shall not offer, give, or receive any bribe, kickback, or improper benefit in connection with this order, in compliance with UAE anti-corruption regulations.`;

